              "output": "[{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"# Exercise: Dengue forecasting\\n\\nData: [DrivenData dengue benchmark](https://drivendata.co/blog/dengue-benchmark/)\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"b6ce810a\"},{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"## Setup\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"2b038968\"},{\"cellType\":\"code\",\"source\":\"library('tidymodels')\\nlibrary('slider')\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"301cfc1b\",\"language\":\"R\"},{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"## Load the data\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"5f8ac8fd\"},{\"cellType\":\"code\",\"source\":\"dengue = readr::read_csv('../data/dengue_features_train.csv', show_col_types = FALSE)\\nlabels = readr::read_csv('../data/dengue_labels_train.csv', show_col_types = FALSE)\\n\\ndengue |> glimpse()\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"77fab22b\",\"language\":\"R\"},{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"## 1. Count the missing values\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Hint</summary>\\n\\n```R\\ndengue |>\\n    summarize(across(everything(), \\\\(x) sum(is.na(x)))) |>\\n    pivot_longer(everything(), names_to = 'column', values_to = 'n_missing') |>\\n    arrange(desc(n_missing))\\n```\\n\\n</details>\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"e3f17ed0\"},{\"cellType\":\"code\",\"source\":\"dengue |>\\n    summarize(across(everything(), \\\\(x) sum(is.na(x)))) |>\\n    pivot_longer(everything(), names_to = 'column', values_to = 'n_missing') |>\\n    arrange(desc(n_missing))\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"cc45fa25\",\"language\":\"R\"},{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"## 2. Fill the missing values\\n\\nSort by date. Fill each city on its own. Keep 4 features. Join the labels.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Hint</summary>\\n\\n```R\\npreprocess_data = function(features, labels = NULL) {\\n    keep = c(\\n        'city', 'year', 'weekofyear', 'week_start_date',\\n        'reanalysis_specific_humidity_g_per_kg',\\n        'reanalysis_dew_point_temp_k',\\n        'station_avg_temp_c',\\n        'station_min_temp_c'\\n    )\\n    df = features |>\\n        select(all_of(keep)) |>\\n        arrange(city, week_start_date) |>\\n        group_by(city) |>\\n        fill(everything(), .direction = 'down') |>\\n        ungroup()\\n    if (!is.null(labels)) {\\n        df = df |> left_join(labels, by = c('city', 'year', 'weekofyear'))\\n    }\\n    df\\n}\\n\\ndengue_processed = preprocess_data(dengue, labels)\\n\\ndengue_processed |> summarize(across(everything(), \\\\(x) sum(is.na(x))))\\n```\\n\\n</details>\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"3cdb5429\"},{\"cellType\":\"code\",\"source\":\"preprocess_data = function(features, labels = NULL) {\\n    keep = c(\\n        'city', 'year', 'weekofyear', 'week_start_date',\\n        'reanalysis_specific_humidity_g_per_kg',\\n        'reanalysis_dew_point_temp_k',\\n        'station_avg_temp_c',\\n        'station_min_temp_c'\\n    )\\n    df = features |>\\n        select(all_of(keep)) |>\\n        arrange(city, week_start_date) |>\\n        group_by(city) |>\\n        fill(everything(), .direction = 'down') |>\\n        ungroup()\\n    if (!is.null(labels)) {\\n        df = df |> left_join(labels, by = c('city', 'year', 'weekofyear'))\\n    }\\n    df\\n}\\n\\ndengue_processed = preprocess_data(dengue, labels)\\n\\ndengue_processed |> summarize(across(everything(), \\\\(x) sum(is.na(x))))\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"caef8853\",\"language\":\"R\"},{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"## 3. Train and test sets, by city\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Hint</summary>\\n\\n```R\\ndengue_sj = dengue_processed |> filter(city == 'sj')\\ndengue_iq = dengue_processed |> filter(city == 'iq')\\n\\nsj_train = dengue_sj |> slice(1:800)\\nsj_test = dengue_sj |> slice(801:n())\\n\\niq_train = dengue_iq |> slice(1:400)\\niq_test = dengue_iq |> slice(401:n())\\n```\\n\\n</details>\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"f1ec12a1\"},{\"cellType\":\"code\",\"source\":\"dengue_sj = dengue_processed |> filter(city == 'sj')\\ndengue_iq = dengue_processed |> filter(city == 'iq')\\n\\nsj_train = dengue_sj |> slice(1:800)\\nsj_test = dengue_sj |> slice(801:n())\\n\\niq_train = dengue_iq |> slice(1:400)\\niq_test = dengue_iq |> slice(401:n())\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"9962ce67\",\"language\":\"R\"},{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"## 4. Random forest, one model per city\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Hint</summary>\\n\\n```R\\nmod = rand_forest(trees = 500, min_n = 30) |> set_mode('regression')\\n\\nformula = total_cases ~ weekofyear + reanalysis_specific_humidity_g_per_kg +\\n    reanalysis_dew_point_temp_k + station_avg_temp_c + station_min_temp_c\\n\\nmod_sj_fit = mod |> fit(formula, data = sj_train)\\n\\nmod_iq_fit = mod |> fit(formula, data = iq_train)\\n```\\n\\n</details>\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"54d2068d\"},{\"cellType\":\"code\",\"source\":\"mod = rand_forest(trees = 500, min_n = 30) |> set_mode('regression')\\n\\nformula = total_cases ~ weekofyear + reanalysis_specific_humidity_g_per_kg +\\n    reanalysis_dew_point_temp_k + station_avg_temp_c + station_min_temp_c\\n\\nmod_sj_fit = mod |> fit(formula, data = sj_train)\\n\\nmod_iq_fit = mod |> fit(formula, data = iq_train)\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"ef7b7bb4\",\"language\":\"R\"},{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"## 5. Plot the test predictions\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Hint</summary>\\n\\n```R\\noptions(repr.plot.width = 10, repr.plot.height = 4, repr.plot.res = 250)\\n\\nsj_test |>\\n    mutate(fitted = predict(mod_sj_fit, new_data = sj_test)$.pred, t = row_number()) |>\\nggplot(aes(x = t)) +\\n    geom_line(aes(y = total_cases, color = 'actual')) +\\n    geom_line(aes(y = fitted, color = 'predicted')) +\\n    labs(x = 'week', y = 'total_cases', color = NULL) +\\n    theme_minimal()\\n```\\n\\n</details>\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"377fa91c\"},{\"cellType\":\"code\",\"source\":\"options(repr.plot.width = 10, repr.plot.height = 4, repr.plot.res = 250)\\n\\nsj_test |>\\n    mutate(fitted = predict(mod_sj_fit, new_data = sj_test)$.pred, t = row_number()) |>\\nggplot(aes(x = t)) +\\n    geom_line(aes(y = total_cases, color = 'actual')) +\\n    geom_line(aes(y = fitted, color = 'predicted')) +\\n    labs(x = 'week', y = 'total_cases', color = NULL) +\\n    theme_minimal()\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"b0405531\",\"language\":\"R\"},{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"## 6. Lag features\\n\\nBuild these per city:\\n\\n- Rolling means (2, 4, 6, 8 weeks) of humidity, dew point, min temp, air temp, precipitation\\n- Cases at t-1, t-2, t-4, and rolling means (4, 8 weeks) of cases up to t-1\\n- `week_sin` and `week_cos`\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Hint</summary>\\n\\n```R\\n# Mean of the last w weeks (this week and the w - 1 before it)\\n# .complete = TRUE gives NA for the first w - 1 weeks, which have too few weeks\\nroll_mean = function(x, w) slider::slide_dbl(x, mean, .before = w - 1, .complete = TRUE)\\n\\nlag_data = dengue |>\\n    select(\\n        city, year, weekofyear, week_start_date,\\n        humidity = reanalysis_specific_humidity_g_per_kg,\\n        dew_point = reanalysis_dew_point_temp_k,\\n        min_temp = station_min_temp_c,\\n        air_temp = reanalysis_air_temp_k,\\n        precip = precipitation_amt_mm\\n    ) |>\\n    left_join(labels, by = c('city', 'year', 'weekofyear')) |>\\n    arrange(city, week_start_date) |>\\n    group_by(city) |>\\n    fill(everything(), .direction = 'down') |>\\n    mutate(\\n        across(\\n            c(humidity, dew_point, min_temp, air_temp, precip),\\n            list(\\n                ma2 = ~roll_mean(.x, 2),\\n                ma4 = ~roll_mean(.x, 4),\\n                ma6 = ~roll_mean(.x, 6),\\n                ma8 = ~roll_mean(.x, 8)\\n            ),\\n            .names = '{.col}_{.fn}'\\n        ),\\n        cases_lag1 = lag(total_cases, 1),\\n        cases_lag2 = lag(total_cases, 2),\\n        cases_lag4 = lag(total_cases, 4),\\n        cases_ma4 = roll_mean(lag(total_cases, 1), 4),\\n        cases_ma8 = roll_mean(lag(total_cases, 1), 8),\\n        week_sin = sin(2 * pi * weekofyear / 52),\\n        week_cos = cos(2 * pi * weekofyear / 52)\\n    ) |>\\n    ungroup() |>\\n    drop_na() |>\\n    # Keep only what the model uses: the rolling means, case lags and season\\n    select(-c(year, week_start_date, humidity, dew_point, min_temp, air_temp, precip))\\n```\\n\\n</details>\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"c07d8af2\"},{\"cellType\":\"code\",\"source\":\"# Mean of the last w weeks (this week and the w - 1 before it)\\n# .complete = TRUE gives NA for the first w - 1 weeks, which have too few weeks\\nroll_mean = function(x, w) slider::slide_dbl(x, mean, .before = w - 1, .complete = TRUE)\\n\\nlag_data = dengue |>\\n    select(\\n        city, year, weekofyear, week_start_date,\\n        humidity = reanalysis_specific_humidity_g_per_kg,\\n        dew_point = reanalysis_dew_point_temp_k,\\n        min_temp = station_min_temp_c,\\n        air_temp = reanalysis_air_temp_k,\\n        precip = precipitation_amt_mm\\n    ) |>\\n    left_join(labels, by = c('city', 'year', 'weekofyear')) |>\\n    arrange(city, week_start_date) |>\\n    group_by(city) |>\\n    fill(everything(), .direction = 'down') |>\\n    mutate(\\n        across(\\n            c(humidity, dew_point, min_temp, air_temp, precip),\\n            list(\\n                ma2 = ~roll_mean(.x, 2),\\n                ma4 = ~roll_mean(.x, 4),\\n                ma6 = ~roll_mean(.x, 6),\\n                ma8 = ~roll_mean(.x, 8)\\n            ),\\n            .names = '{.col}_{.fn}'\\n        ),\\n        cases_lag1 = lag(total_cases, 1),\\n        cases_lag2 = lag(total_cases, 2),\\n        cases_lag4 = lag(total_cases, 4),\\n        cases_ma4 = roll_mean(lag(total_cases, 1), 4),\\n        cases_ma8 = roll_mean(lag(total_cases, 1), 8),\\n        week_sin = sin(2 * pi * weekofyear / 52),\\n        week_cos = cos(2 * pi * weekofyear / 52)\\n    ) |>\\n    ungroup() |>\\n    drop_na() |>\\n    # Keep only what the model uses: the rolling means, case lags and season\\n    select(-c(year, week_start_date, humidity, dew_point, min_temp, air_temp, precip))\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"836e7e55\",\"language\":\"R\"},{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"## 7. Train and test sets for the lag features\\n\\nUse the same test size as before.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Hint</summary>\\n\\n```R\\nsplit_city = function(city_name, n_test) {\\n    d = lag_data |> filter(city == city_name) |> select(-city)\\n    list(\\n        train = d |> slice(1:(n() - n_test)),\\n        test = d |> slice((n() - n_test + 1):n())\\n    )\\n}\\n\\nsj_lag_split = split_city('sj', nrow(sj_test))\\niq_lag_split = split_city('iq', nrow(iq_test))\\n```\\n\\n</details>\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"6e5a93fa\"},{\"cellType\":\"code\",\"source\":\"split_city = function(city_name, n_test) {\\n    d = lag_data |> filter(city == city_name) |> select(-city)\\n    list(\\n        train = d |> slice(1:(n() - n_test)),\\n        test = d |> slice((n() - n_test + 1):n())\\n    )\\n}\\n\\nsj_lag_split = split_city('sj', nrow(sj_test))\\niq_lag_split = split_city('iq', nrow(iq_test))\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"11632b45\",\"language\":\"R\"},{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"## 8. Random forest with lag features\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Hint</summary>\\n\\n```R\\n# `total_cases ~ .` uses every other column in the data\\nmod_sj_lag_fit = mod |> fit(total_cases ~ ., data = sj_lag_split$train)\\n\\nmod_iq_lag_fit = mod |> fit(total_cases ~ ., data = iq_lag_split$train)\\n```\\n\\n</details>\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"d3cc2663\"},{\"cellType\":\"code\",\"source\":\"# `total_cases ~ .` uses every other column in the data\\nmod_sj_lag_fit = mod |> fit(total_cases ~ ., data = sj_lag_split$train)\\n\\nmod_iq_lag_fit = mod |> fit(total_cases ~ ., data = iq_lag_split$train)\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"648afbdb\",\"language\":\"R\"},{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"## 9. Compare the test error (MAE)\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Hint</summary>\\n\\n```R\\nmae = function(fit, test) mean(abs(predict(fit, new_data = test)$.pred - test$total_cases))\\n\\ntibble(\\n    city = c('sj', 'iq'),\\n    baseline = c(mae(mod_sj_fit, sj_test), mae(mod_iq_fit, iq_test)),\\n    lag_features = c(mae(mod_sj_lag_fit, sj_lag_split$test), mae(mod_iq_lag_fit, iq_lag_split$test))\\n)\\n```\\n\\n</details>\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"36b78a2d\"},{\"cellType\":\"code\",\"source\":\"mae = function(fit, test) mean(abs(predict(fit, new_data = test)$.pred - test$total_cases))\\n\\ntibble(\\n    city = c('sj', 'iq'),\\n    baseline = c(mae(mod_sj_fit, sj_test), mae(mod_iq_fit, iq_test)),\\n    lag_features = c(mae(mod_sj_lag_fit, sj_lag_split$test), mae(mod_iq_lag_fit, iq_lag_split$test))\\n)\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"19fd5de7\",\"language\":\"R\"},{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"## 10. Plot the comparison\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Hint</summary>\\n\\n```R\\nplot_compare = function(fit_base, test_base, fit_lag, test_lag, title) {\\n    tibble(\\n        t = seq_len(nrow(test_lag)),\\n        actual = test_lag$total_cases,\\n        baseline = predict(fit_base, new_data = test_base)$.pred,\\n        lag_features = predict(fit_lag, new_data = test_lag)$.pred\\n    ) |>\\n        pivot_longer(-t) |>\\n        ggplot(aes(t, value, color = name)) +\\n        geom_line() +\\n        labs(title = title, x = 'week', y = 'total_cases', color = NULL) +\\n        theme_minimal()\\n}\\n\\nplot_compare(mod_sj_fit, sj_test, mod_sj_lag_fit, sj_lag_split$test, 'San Juan')\\nplot_compare(mod_iq_fit, iq_test, mod_iq_lag_fit, iq_lag_split$test, 'Iquitos')\\n```\\n\\n</details>\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"0d7e4eda\"},{\"cellType\":\"code\",\"source\":\"plot_compare = function(fit_base, test_base, fit_lag, test_lag, title) {\\n    tibble(\\n        t = seq_len(nrow(test_lag)),\\n        actual = test_lag$total_cases,\\n        baseline = predict(fit_base, new_data = test_base)$.pred,\\n        lag_features = predict(fit_lag, new_data = test_lag)$.pred\\n    ) |>\\n        pivot_longer(-t) |>\\n        ggplot(aes(t, value, color = name)) +\\n        geom_line() +\\n        labs(title = title, x = 'week', y = 'total_cases', color = NULL) +\\n        theme_minimal()\\n}\\n\\nplot_compare(mod_sj_fit, sj_test, mod_sj_lag_fit, sj_lag_split$test, 'San Juan')\\nplot_compare(mod_iq_fit, iq_test, mod_iq_lag_fit, iq_lag_split$test, 'Iquitos')\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"9505d924\",\"language\":\"R\"},{\"cellType\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"## Bonus: variable importance\\n\\nMake a `vip` chart of the San Juan model with lag features. Which columns matter most?\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Hint</summary>\\n\\n```R\\n# importance = 'impurity' tells ranger to keep track of importance\\nmod_imp = mod |> set_engine('ranger', importance = 'impurity')\\n\\nmod_sj_imp_fit = mod_imp |> fit(total_cases ~ ., data = sj_lag_split$train)\\n\\nvip::vip(mod_sj_imp_fit)\\n```\\n\\n</details>\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"f9bb82cd\"},{\"cellType\":\"code\",\"source\":\"\\nmod_imp = mod |> set_engine('ranger', importance = 'impurity')\\n\\nmod_sj_imp_fit = mod_imp |> fit(total_cases ~ ., data = sj_lag_split$train)\\n\\nvip::vip(mod_sj_imp_fit)\",\"execution_count\":null,\"cell_id\":\"048efb1e\",\"language\":\"R\"}]",
              "metadata": {
