      "body": "All 13 code cells are completed and the notebook runs cleanly with no errors.\n\nFilled in each empty cell (steps 1\u201310 + bonus) using the provided hints, then ran everything:\n\n- **Missing values** counted, then filled per city with `fill(... 'down')` \u2014 after preprocessing all counts are 0 \u2713\n- **Train/test splits** per city (sj 800/rest, iq 400/rest)\n- **Baseline random forest** per city (`weekofyear` + 4 weather features)\n- **Lag features**: rolling means (2/4/6/8 wk), case lags (1/2/4), case rolling means, `week_sin`/`week_cos`\n- **Lag-feature random forests** and MAE comparison \u2014 lag features beat baseline for both cities (sj 21.4\u219210.0, iq 6.5\u21925.3) \u2713\n- **Bonus** `vip` importance chart for San Juan\n\nTwo setup items were needed to run it:\n- Installed `r-ranger` and `r-vip` via `pixi add` (the notebook's RF engine).\n- Downloaded the data (not in the repo) to `/workspaces/codespace/data/`: `dengue_features_train.csv` and `dengue_labels_train.csv`.",
